<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal November retail sales rose yr/yr 2.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal November retail sales rose yr/yr 2.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's retail sales index rose just 0.1 percent in November from the previous month, but retail sales were 2.9 percent up on November 1995, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>INE gave the following figures for retail sales:</p>
<p>				     Nov 96	 Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)	   151.5	   151.3	  147.3</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (pct)	    2.9	    5.8	    2.9</p>
<p>Components:</p>
<p>    Food and drink		168.1	   169.0	  172.7</p>
<p>    Chemical/pharmaceutical   174.8	   185.4	  164.9</p>
<p>    Clothing/footwear/textile 246.3	   206.3	  242.5</p>
<p>    Furniture		     134.9	   119.6	  117.6</p>
<p>    Construction materials    129.2	   147.8	  136.1</p>
<p>    Vehicles			110.6	   117.6	   99.0</p>
<p>    Fuel			    151.2	   153.0	  142.4</p>
<p>    Warehouse/market sales    133.9	   139.3	  129.8</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
